course: dictionary
lesson: 5518
title: One word, many meanings: lean
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word lean can mean different things. Its meaning depends on the words around it, which is its context. When you see lean, ask: is someone bending, resting, depending on someone, or describing something as thin?
explain: To lean is to bend your body towards something or away from straight: «Lean forward». To lean on or against something is to rest your weight on it. «The boy leaned on a glass case to see better.» Here, leaned on means rested his weight on the case.
explain: To lean on someone means to depend on them for help. Lean can also be an adjective, a describing word. It means thin and fit, or, for meat, having little fat. «Lean meat has little fat.» Check the clues: the words after lean tell you which meaning you need.
fact: Lean is a verb (action word) and also an adjective (describing word).
fact: To lean is to bend your body towards something or away from straight.
fact: To lean on or against something is to rest your weight on it.
fact: To lean on someone means to depend on them for help.
fact: Lean as an adjective means thin and fit, or having little fat when it describes meat.
exercise: «Lean forward to see the board better.» What does lean mean here? | *To bend your body towards something | To shout loudly | To stop eating meat | To run very fast
exercise: «The boy leaned on the glass case to see better.» What does leaned on mean? | *Rested his weight on it | Painted it bright blue | Hit it very hard | Ran away from it
exercise: Mum says, «Never lean out of the window.» Why is this a safety rule? | Because it is hot outside | *Because you could fall | Because windows are too heavy to open | Because it is rude
test: «Lean meat has little fat.» What does lean mean in this sentence? | *Having little fat | Lost in thought | Very cold | Very tall
test: Ella says, «I lean on my big sister when I feel stuck.» What does lean on mean here? | To hit someone | To forget something | To move to the left | *To depend on someone for help
exam: «Nadia likes to lean towards the quieter games.» What does lean towards mean here? | To run very fast | To fall over | To sing loudly | *To prefer
